cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "ReduLink: Context-Bound Reference Substitution over Encrypted QUIC Streams"
message: "If you use ReduLink, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Nguyen
    given-names: Michél
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6834-4422"
    affiliation: "University of the People"
year: 2026
version: "3.16"
repository-code: "https://github.com/pinkysworld/redulink-deduplex-quic"
abstract: "ReduLink studies when context-bound reference substitution can reduce application-stream bytes between cooperating QUIC endpoints with explicit warm state. The v3.16 artifact adds matching live TLS 1.3 exporter derivation, an exact miss-cost deployment envelope with a separate residency gate, authenticated FULL and REF records, bounded true-LRU state, validated batched repair, exact reconstruction, and same-layer baselines. Single-host results support byte, exporter-binding, and state-machine claims, not WAN latency, congestion fairness, workload prevalence, or production throughput."
keywords:
  - QUIC
  - redundancy elimination
  - deduplication
  - reference substitution
  - transport protocols
license: MIT
